('h1', '4. Machine Learning for Battery State Estimation'),
('p',
 "SOC estimation is the most mature BMS function, and the corpus shows how machine learning entered it. The early pattern pairs learning with classical estimation: Gaussian process regression for pack-level SOC with native uncertainty quantification [[10.1016/j.energy.2020.118000]], and \u2014 most influentially \u2014 recurrent networks embedded in unscented Kalman filters, where the LSTM supplies a learned observation model and the filter recursive correction [[10.1016/j.energy.2020.117664]]. A second generation tuned network structure itself: particle-swarm-optimized LSTM improved accuracy and noise robustness [[10.1016/j.energy.2021.121236]], and evolutionary-assisted CNN\u2013BiLSTM hybrids report sub-1% drive-cycle errors [[10.1016/j.heliyon.2024.e35183]]. Simulation-informed training pipelines substitute automotive-accurate simulated data for exhaustive cell testing [[10.1016/j.jpowsour.2020.229108]], comparative benchmarks on standard drive cycles weigh ML regression families [[10.3390/wevj12010038]], pack heterogeneity is addressed by joint pack-SOC and cell-inconsistency estimation with balancing-aware formulations [[10.1109/access.2021.3068776]], and unified frameworks estimate SOH and SOC jointly from partial charging data [[10.1016/j.ensm.2022.06.053]], and large-format applications extend estimation to containerized storage strings [[10.1016/j.jpowsour.2024.235609]], with comparative benchmarks weighing accuracy against embedded compute budgets [[10.1016/j.est.2024.114281]][[10.1016/j.est.2024.111877]]."),
('p',
 "The most substantive recent shift is toward hybrid schemes in which a filter, an equivalent-circuit model, or a physics prior constrains the learner: GA-optimized LSTM coupled with improved adaptive Kalman filtering reaches low error under measurement noise that breaks pure-network estimators [[10.1016/j.apenergy.2024.123508]]; equivalent-circuit-informed ML on impedance features estimates SOC across temperatures [[10.1016/j.energy.2023.128461]]; and physics-informed recurrent structures embed battery dynamics directly into the training objective [[10.1109/jrfid.2022.3211841]]. These schemes trade engineering complexity for extrapolation behavior \u2014 the property that matters most onboard. Yet 13 of the 17 corpus SOC papers rest on laboratory-scale data and 12 on a single chemistry, and only one demonstrates fleet-scale operation [[10.1016/j.jpowsour.2024.235609]]; benchmark heterogeneity makes cross-paper comparison nearly meaningless [[10.1016/j.egyai.2025.100585]][[10.20517/jmi.2024.84]]. The laboratory problem is largely solved; the deployment problem \u2014 guaranteed accuracy on arbitrary packs over full aging \u2014 is not."),

('h1', '5. Machine Learning for Health Estimation and Prognostics'),
('p',
 "SOH estimation and RUL prediction form the largest functional block of the corpus (35 papers). The founding pattern is classical: extract health-sensitive features from partial charge or discharge curves, then regress with Gaussian process or similar shallow models \u2014 incremental-capacity analysis with explicit uncertainty bounds [[10.1016/j.energy.2019.116467]], differential thermal voltammetry [[10.1109/tte.2020.3028784]], and Gaussian-process classification of impedance spectra that identifies degradation modes [[10.1038/s41467-020-15235-7]], and deep Gaussian processes coupling prognosis with degradation-mode identification [[10.1016/j.jpowsour.2019.227281]]. Measurement relaxations followed: random partial charging data proved sufficient for accurate SOH [[10.1109/tpel.2021.3134701]], and charging-segment adjustment refined features for vehicle-level use [[10.1016/j.apenergy.2024.124077]]. The landmark systematization is Roman et al.'s 179-cell pipeline showing that relaxed charge-curve features support accurate SOH estimation across a heterogeneous commercial fleet [[10.1038/s42256-021-00312-3]]."),
('p',
 "Deep architectures entered as sequence models over capacity-fade trajectories and representation learners over raw curves: graph convolutional networks fusing multiple health indicators [[10.1016/j.ress.2022.108947]], graph networks over partial discharge curves [[10.1016/j.est.2024.113502]], BiLSTM\u2013Transformer hybrids under fast-charging stress [[10.1016/j.energy.2024.133418]], hybrid-fusion networks for real-time prediction streams [[10.1016/j.energy.2025.136618]], and interpretable deep learning with transparency mechanisms [[10.1016/j.apenergy.2024.124713]]. Field-data studies absorb real-vehicle noise [[10.1016/j.energy.2023.126855]] and estimate pack-level SOH from fleet streams [[10.1016/j.geits.2024.100169]], while deep models estimate SOH without additional degradation experiments by learning trajectory features that generalize across chemistries [[10.1038/s41467-023-38458-w]]. Early-life prediction \u2014 forecasting lifetime from the first cycles \u2014 compresses test times from months to days [[10.1038/s41560-019-0356-8]][[10.1016/j.apenergy.2021.116897]][[10.1016/j.energy.2021.120205]], hybrid physics-plus-learned models give early RUL from limited cycles [[10.1016/j.jclepro.2021.128265]], extends to lithium-metal chemistries [[10.1002/advs.202402608]], and now runs on embedded boards in real time [[10.1016/j.est.2022.104901]]."),
('p',
 "The prognostics cluster shows the clearest physics-informed turn: physics-informed online degradation models [[10.1016/j.ymssp.2022.109347]], hybrid reinforcement learning that reduces the data demand of SOH estimation [[10.1038/s41598-025-30602-4]], a generalizable PINN from limited early-cycle data [[10.1016/j.jechem.2025.08.093]], EIS-informed physics-constrained networks [[10.1016/j.energy.2025.139753]], a generic physics-informed RUL framework for small early-life samples [[10.1016/j.apenergy.2025.125314]], multi-feature hybrids across datasets [[10.1016/j.est.2025.118415]], recurrent networks anticipating uncertain duty [[10.1016/j.ensm.2022.05.007]], and signal-decomposition hybrids on noisy capacity series [[10.1038/s41598-025-92262-8]]. Transfer learning attacks generalization directly: domain-adversarial training across operating conditions [[10.1109/tpel.2021.3117788]], deep transfer with partial charging curves across cell types [[10.1016/j.energy.2023.127033]], transfer under fast-charging protocols [[10.1016/j.isci.2025.112235]], cross-chemistry EIS estimation [[10.1109/tte.2025.3533540]], and a general framework quantifying the laboratory-to-fleet domain gap [[10.1016/j.apenergy.2024.125086]]. The critical assessment: accuracy claims cluster around 1\u20132% SOH error, but they are established overwhelmingly on public benchmark cells \u2014 10 of the 35 studies in this complex use within-cell or k-fold validation (17 corpus-wide) \u2014 and the transfer-learning papers, the honest exception, reveal how much shift remains unaddressed. SOH estimation under controlled conditions is approaching incremental returns; calibrated lifetime and safety margins for arbitrary packs in the field remain open [[10.1016/j.joule.2019.11.018]][[10.1016/j.jechem.2023.03.026]]."),

('tbl', 'TABLE_REP'),

('h1', '6. Machine Learning for Charging Control and Optimization'),
('p',
 "Charging control is the function where machine learning has changed experimental practice most directly. The defining result is Attia et al.: a Bayesian optimization loop identified fast-charging protocols within 2.5 months, against roughly 18 months of manual search [[10.1038/s41586-020-1994-5]]. Ensemble surrogates make multi-objective strategy optimization tractable [[10.1016/j.enconman.2025.120170]], and Bayesian fast-charging optimization reduces charge time under degradation constraints [[10.1109/tte.2023.3311813]]. A second line embeds degradation mechanisms into the decision itself: machine-learning fast charging that perceives and regulates internal lithium-plating onset enables plating-free rapid protocols [[10.1016/j.ensm.2022.12.034]], adaptive multistage schemes adjust stage boundaries against measured degradation [[10.1016/j.renene.2019.08.077]], module-level optimization manages temperature gradients [[10.1016/j.energy.2022.126331]], and pack-level extensions coordinate balance-aware charging [[10.1016/j.est.2024.111755]][[10.1016/j.est.2024.112046]]."),
('p',
 "The deployment gap is most concrete here: of the eight charging papers, one is a large-scale closed-loop hardware campaign, three validate on laboratory hardware, and the rest are simulation-only. The unsolved problem is certifiable learning-based charging \u2014 which is why mechanism-aware schemes such as plating-perception control [[10.1016/j.ensm.2022.12.034]] are the cluster's most deployment-relevant results."),

('h1', '7. Machine Learning for Thermal Management, Faults and Safety'),
('p',
 "Thermal management (8 papers) divides by purpose. For estimation, ANN models predict cell temperature across operating conditions [[10.1016/j.applthermaleng.2023.120482]] and internal-temperature sensing extends to ultrahigh-rate discharge where surface measurement fails [[10.1016/j.apenergy.2026.127394]]. For design, ML surrogates amortize expensive CFD evaluation across optimization loops [[10.1016/j.jpowsour.2021.229727]][[10.1016/j.applthermaleng.2024.123826]], with experimentally validated parallel-liquid-cooling designs closing the loop [[10.1016/j.applthermaleng.2022.118503]]. For control, ANN controllers demonstrate parasitic-load reductions in simulation [[10.3390/wevj16050279]] \u2014 but no corpus paper closes this loop on hardware, leaving thermal control where charging control was five years ago. Physics-informed heat-generation estimation embeds thermal priors into the learning problem [[10.1016/j.jechem.2022.11.036]], and the cluster is consolidated by a state-of-the-art review [[10.1016/j.est.2023.106688]]."),
('p',
 "Fault and safety applications (9 papers) divide into diagnosis of realized faults and prediction of impending hazards: grid-search-optimized SVMs classify sensor and connection faults [[10.1016/j.energy.2020.118866]], curvilinear-distance methods detect multiple pack fault types in operating fleets [[10.1016/j.est.2023.107575]], and multi-scenario deep anomaly detection covers real EV operating envelopes [[10.1016/j.etran.2025.100418]]; force-signal deep learning catches lithium-plating-type defects at manufacturing [[10.1016/j.jechem.2025.04.025]]. The hazard-prediction side is increasingly model-based: multiphysics models coupled with ML predict module-level thermal-runaway progression [[10.1016/j.jpowsour.2024.235015]], a multiphysics-informed DeepONet augments scarce experimental events with virtual data [[10.1016/j.etran.2024.100337]], and multi-source domain transfer moves thermal-runaway diagnosis across fleets with small target samples [[10.1016/j.apenergy.2024.123248]]. The reviews in this cluster are candid that laboratory fault diagnosis has historically failed to transfer to real vehicles [[10.1016/j.etran.2023.100254]][[10.3390/electronics10111309]]; the fleet-data anomaly-detection studies are therefore the cluster's most valuable trend, even though label scarcity for rare faults keeps evaluation largely qualitative."),

